---
import Layout from '@/components/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '@/lib/site';
import { TOOL_COUNT } from '@/lib/registry';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description={`What ${site.name} is, how it works, and how to install it as an app on any platform.`}
  path="/about"
  narrow
>
  <article class="prose-tool max-w-prose">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[rgb(var(--text))] sm:text-3xl">
      About {site.name}
    </h1>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a growing collection of {TOOL_COUNT} small utilities, encoders, hashers, formatters,
      converters, generators, image and PDF helpers, that all run on your device. It exists because the
      common "online tool" pattern of uploading a file to a stranger's server is unnecessary for most
      of these tasks: the browser can do them itself.
    </p>

    <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
    <p>
      The site is fully static. Each tool is a self-contained module that is only downloaded when
      you open it, so the app stays small. Heavier jobs run in a Web Worker so the interface never
      freezes. There is no backend.
    </p>

    <h2 id="install">Install as an app</h2>
    <p>{site.name} is a Progressive Web App and installs on every major platform:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Chrome / Edge (desktop)</strong>: click the install icon in the address bar, or menu
        more "Install {site.shortName}".
      </li>
      <li><strong>Android (Chrome)</strong>: menu "Add to Home screen" or "Install app".</li>
      <li><strong>iOS / iPadOS (Safari)</strong>: Share "Add to Home Screen".</li>
      <li><strong>macOS (Safari 17+)</strong>: File "Add to Dock".</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Firefox</strong>: there is no install prompt, so pin the tab or use the site in a
        dedicated window.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Once installed it opens in its own window and works with no internet connection.</p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      The code is MIT-licensed and available <a href={site.repository} rel="noopener">on GitHub</a>.
      Issues and tool suggestions are welcome. Adding a tool is intentionally small. See the
      <a href={`${site.repository}/blob/main/docs/ADDING-A-TOOL.md`} rel="noopener"
        >adding-a-tool guide</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      These tools are provided as-is. For anything safety-critical (legal, financial, medical),
      verify results independently.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
